 what was that guy  called Camilla Camilla parker-bowles  Billy Ray Cyrus I remember it's Haley  Joel Osment anyway all of this history  changing has resulted in more funding  going to the space program creating  amongst other things a space research  facility known as Talos 1 this is where  things go off the rails within your  first 30 minutes you realize you are not  on earth but in fact you're on Talos 1  does that mean you work at an  intergalactic space research facility or  are you the one receiving the research  so to speak smashing a window for the  first time to see reality is quite  impactful so don't watch that bit you  just watched sorry  after the tension has been built up for  about 10 minutes you finally meet the  mimics which are the baseline enemy in  this game but they do live up to their  names  if that happened a little bit too fast  let's have another look again the mimics  aerospace parasite that can mimic  objects in their surroundings so this  little blighter hid in plain sight as a  coffee mug think about what this means  when you play through isn't that bin a  bin or is it a mimic is that chair  really a chair this simple enemy will  scare the hell out of you over and over  again and this is just one of many  enemies wait till you meet these buggers  you'll notice many dead humans with  haggard looks on their faces and when  you do remember this scary fact  [Applause]  [Music]  aash one human plus one mimic equals one  dead human and four mimics it's gonna be  a tough ride so how do you fight these  little monstrosity x' well with weapons  of course starting with a trusty wrench  like the crowbar you had back in  half-life you can squish mimics you face  but bigger enemies require bigger guns  shotguns work a treat but look at the  glue cannon this is like a militarized  expanding form weapon which sticks to  and freezes enemies where they stand  allowing you to show them who's boss the  glue cannon also can create makeshift  bridges walkways making it invaluable if  you played Bioshock you'll be happy to  know that plasmids are here okay they're  not exactly the same but in terms of  upgrades prey borrows a great deal from  the Bioshock trilogy neuro mods are  praised way of ascending Morgan's  abilities in three core areas scientist  engineer security engineering is based  around modding and repairing your  weaponry security is more about what  your character can physically do and  scientists is for health upgrades and  using specialized lab equipment so when  can we get our hands on prey not long at  all it is scheduled for release the day  after Starr was there May the fifth what  do you think of prey not bothered never  seen it before or you can't wait to play  it or maybe you're looking forward with  healthy skepticism please let me know  below a like will be hugely appreciated  and maybe think about subscribing to our  little Channel I imagine from  PlayStation grenade I'll see you next  time  [Music]

